+# crm_bot Codex MVP Work-Item Bundle
+
+This bundle turns the Pilot v0.1 release package into an executable Codex workflow.
+
+It adds:
+
+- a mandatory work-item execution contract;
+- three repository skills;
+- two read-only Codex subagents;
+- a strict MVP work-item workflow;
+- an executable backlog with S1.1 through S1.7 task cards;
+- QA-design and acceptance-evidence records;
+- integration addenda for `AGENTS.md` and the existing implementation workflow;
+- an installer that copies new files and appends integration blocks idempotently.
+
+## Design principle
+
+A user prompt selects the backlog item. The repository defines what correct execution means.
+
+The required lifecycle is:
+
+`approved specification -> backlog card -> QA design -> impact/architecture plan -> tests first -> minimal implementation -> independent acceptance -> documentation/evidence sync -> one atomic commit`
+
+## Important initial state
+
+The supplied S1 task cards use:
+
+- `status: ready_for_qa_design`;
+- `implementation_gate: blocked_until_required_adrs_accepted`.
+
+QA design may proceed while ADR-0002 and ADR-0003 are proposed. Production implementation may not start until every ADR listed by the task card is `accepted`.
+
+## Installation
+
+Read `INSTALL.md`, then run `install.sh` from WSL or Linux.
+
+## Normal command after installation
+
+```text
+Выполни backlog item S1.1 по mvp-work-item workflow.
+После полного green gate обнови документацию, создай evidence record и сделай один commit. Не push.
+```
